<v Mike>And, um, I, I guess like, is that necessary?

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:23.080
<v Mike>Like I did not look into this comic at all because I didn't feel like, I don't feel like

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.200
<v Mike>a, it doesn't feel like a licensed thing.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.020
<v Mike>Like, yeah, I could be inspired by that, but is it really like enough of a thing?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.180
<v Mike>Like it just, this kind of feels like a standalone game.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:36.000
<v Mike>You don't need to know any other material other than the fact that the civil war happened.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:43.480
<v Sean>Well, I think that's why, unlike a lot of situations where, you know, a game would be based on a property

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:49.760
